From 1faa3c35504fc3bb6fd759471dae81671baa6a5f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Junction 2026 team <junction2026@localhost>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 03:34:26 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 2/9] feat(backend): label state snapshots as defective or
 good, with a comment

For anomaly detection, every snapshot now has a label, saved in its
state.json and in snapshots.csv:

- POST /api/projects/{id}/state_snapshots takes an optional JSON body
  {"defective": bool = false, "comment": str = ""}; the comment is trimmed,
  at most 500 characters, without NUL; unknown fields are refused (400).
- PATCH /api/projects/{id}/state_snapshots/{snapshot_id} changes defective,
  comment or both (at least one) in state.json (with label_updated_at) and
  rewrites the CSV; 404 state_snapshot_not_found for an unknown snapshot.
- GET /api/projects/{id}/state_snapshots/snapshots.csv downloads the index,
  checked and rebuilt first if needed (?rebuild=true forces it).
- GET /api/projects/{id}/state_snapshots returns defective and comment, and
  takes ?limit= for the newest only.

A capture whose CSV row cannot be written is still saved, with a warning; the
next check of the index adds it. Snapshots from before labels read as good,
without a comment.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
